        <h2>Summary / Description</h2>
        <div class="description">
          OBJECTIVES: <br>
Investigators sought to study the efficacy of medication against signs and symptoms of motion sickness. 
<p>
APPROACH:<br>
Subjects were placed in either a drug or controlled group. The medication group required a three day loading period prior to the test week.  They were asked to take one capsule every eight hours for three days.  Subjects were asked to record any side effects.  They were also asked to monitor sugar levels in their urine by using test strips four times a day.
<p>
RESULTS:<br>
Summarized results aren’t available for this study.
<p>
